From f82e6b67f9b4b2e71e4846b351da178b1fdce890 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Remora <remora@local>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 19:32:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Remora: forward-port black (AMOLED) theme toggle to AOSP 17
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces upstream 0063 (Settings: support black theme for dark mode), which
cannot apply: AOSP 17 rewrote DarkModeScreen's preference hierarchy to named
arguments and added a purpose= field to every PreferenceCategory, so the whole
region the Lineage patch anchors on changed shape.

Almost all of that conflict is context, not content. Lineage's actual
contribution to this file is ONE line — placing DarkModeBlackThemePreference
between the dark-theme-version category and the timing category — so only that
line is carried forward onto AOSP's rewritten hierarchy. Taking "theirs"
wholesale would have reverted both categories to the AOSP 16 positional form.

The two new classes (DarkModeBlackThemePreference, DarkModeBlackThemeStorage)
and the cm_strings.xml additions apply cleanly and are unchanged from upstream.
darkModeStorage is already a member of BaseDarkModeScreen, so the constructor
call needs nothing new in scope.

NOT COMPILE-VERIFIED — written while a build held the tree, so it has not been
through kotlinc.
